57bm-i1b"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-i1b"],"id":"long.record-257bm-i1b","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.90 (The next quotient sum)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.90, p. 70, label record:257bm-i1b","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For a fixed finite set $D\\subseteq\\{2,3,\\ldots\\}$ and $M\\ge0$,\n$$\nQ(D,M+1)=2Q(D,M)+c_D(M+1).\n$$\nThis is the sum of Theorem 6.89 over $d\\in D$. Keeping $D$ fixed is essential: changing the support between steps adds a separate difference of quotient sums. The exclusion of $d=1$ is also essential for the displayed correction term, since $q(M,1)=2^M$ doubles without an added unit.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.record-257bm-i1b","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.record-257bm-i1b","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i1b%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.localPrefixQuotient_succ%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i1b%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.localPrefixQuotient_succ%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.localPrefixQuotient_succ"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/evidence/mapping.long.record-257bm-i1b","id":"field:0b15ebe847b59857b5b0f5e691f5f77187e9ba42b93823ddb717a0bda602ac6b","kind":"subject_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/evidence/mapping.long.record-257bm-i1b","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"subject_ids","to":